# Local scripts and the backend's selection pipeline (packages/backend/src/pipeline) call the model.
# Never commit .env.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Backend pipeline (optional): REVIEW_MODEL (default gpt-4.1-mini-2025-04-14); REVIEW_GATE=strict to
# admit only candidates from VALID strict reviews to the bench; roster rules still govern activation.
# Default basic only handles INSUFFICIENT_EVIDENCE (docs/ops/DEPLOY.md "Selection pipeline").
# Hyperliquid read routing (optional, docs/ops/DEPLOY.md "NOWNodes routing"): set NOWNODES_API_KEY and a non-official mode,
# INFO_ROUTING=official (code default) | overflow (NOWNodes only when the official API fails)
# | split (INFO_SPLIT_PERCENT, default 25, of NOWNodes-capable reads go to NOWNodes first);
# NOWNodes-first profile: INFO_ROUTING=split, INFO_SPLIT_PERCENT=100, NOWNODES_PROBE=on.
# Leave SNAPSHOT_VERIFY off with that profile: its second reader is also NOWNodes.
# INFO_SHADOW_PERCENT=N compares N% of official clearinghouseState reads with NOWNodes in the background.
NOWNODES_API_KEY=
# Optional, all off by default and each needs the key: NOWNODES_PROBE=on probes which info methods NOWNodes serves;
# SNAPSHOT_VERIFY=on|strict cross-checks every mirror snapshot against NOWNodes (SNAPSHOT_VERIFY_TOLERANCE_PCT, default 1).
# CONTRACT_CHECK=on records which picks are contracts on HyperEVM (eth_getCode via NOWNodes; evidence only).
